1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,000
In this tutorial video, we use the Doshi Marvelous Designer 11 version.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:17,000
If you need to learn Marvelous Designer 10 and other version software, please watch the previous video.

3
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:23,000
In order to make it easier to learn, the Doshi Marvelous Designer 11 version is used in this tutorial.

4
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:29,000
In Marvelous Designer, you can use multiple line tools in 3D or 2D windows to merge the version.

5
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:35,000
In this video, we will learn how to use the sewing tool in 3D window to merge the costume.

6
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:45,000
By merging the basic version in 3D window, you will learn how to merge the costume and help you understand how to sew in the 2D window.

7
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Open the project file you saved before.

8
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:57,000
This T-shirt is very simple, we use the line sewing tool to complete all the creation of the sewing line.

9
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:59,000
For other sewing line tools,

10
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:05,000
we will explain in the next tutorial.

11
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:09,000
Put your mouse on the 3D window editor sewing line tool.

12
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Select the line sewing tool in the drop-down menu.

13
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:19,000
The line sewing tool is used to create the sewing line between the lines.

14
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:21,000
You can only choose one line at a time.

15
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:25,000
You can't choose a line made up of multiple lines.

16
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:33,000
As long as you click two lines at a time, you can merge them together.

17
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:35,000
It's very simple.

18
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:39,000
Please note that all sewing lines have their own direction of merging.

19
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:41,000
This will affect the effect of the sewing line.

20
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:43,000
Therefore, when you click to create the sewing line,

21
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:46,000
you should pay attention to the position of the click.

22
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:50,000
As a reference, I first click a line near the top of the mouse,

23
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:53,000
and then click another line near the bottom of the mouse.

24
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:55,000
The created sewing line is crossed.

25
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:57,000
The reason for the crossing of the sewing line is that

26
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:59,000
the position of the mouse click does not match,

27
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:01,000
and the mixing direction is opposite.

28
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:04,000
First, create the sewing line in the front and back.

29
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:08,000
Pay attention to the 2D window.

30
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:10,000
After creating the sewing line,

31
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:14,000
you can see that the sewing line appears in the 2D window at the same time.

32
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:16,000
If you are doing more complicated clothing,

33
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:18,000
the 3D sewing line tool will help you

34
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:25,000
create the right sewing line faster and more clearly.

35
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:27,000
Create the front and back of the sewing line.

36
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:31,000
Pay attention to the 2D window at the side of the sewing line.

37
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:33,000
After we create the sewing line on one side,

38
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:35,000
the other side will also automatically create the sewing line,

39
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:38,000
because the front and back pieces have their own symmetrical panels.

40
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:40,000
Please observe the 2D window to understand

41
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:44,000
which of the two side sewing lines is the only one to be sewn.

42
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:46,000
Continue to complete the shoulder sewing line,

43
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:49,000
pay attention to the direction of matching.

44
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:52,000
Next is the sleeve sewing line.

45
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:56,000
We will learn how the sleeve is combined with the large panel.

46
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:59,000
Click on the sleeve on the front,

47
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:01,000
then click on the corresponding sleeve,

48
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:03,000
then open the 2D window.

49
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:05,000
After opening the 2D window,

50
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:07,000
select the angle to the back,

51
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:10,000
complete the sewing line of the back sleeve and the back sleeve.

52
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:13,000
Now I believe you already understand

53
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:15,000
why we created these panels

54
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:17,000
when we used the column symmetrical panel function,

55
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:19,000
because this way we can save the time

56
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:21,000
to create the other side of the sewing line.

57
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:23,000
Then click on the sleeve,

58
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:25,000
then click on the sleeve,

59
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:28,000
then click on the sleeve,

60
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:30,000
then click on the sleeve,

61
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:32,000
then click on the sleeve,

62
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:34,000
and then click on the sleeve,

63
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:37,000
and then click on the sleeve.

64
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:42,000
Next, we will create the sleeve seam line.

65
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:43,000
After creating the sewing line,

66
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:47,000
turn the angle to see if there are any missed sewing lines.

67
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:52,000
Then we will complete the pocket sewing line.

68
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:53,000
Click on the sewing line

69
00:03:53,000 --> 00:04:03,000
After adding all the powder lines, press the control button to start the simulation and put the costume on the virtual model.

70
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:16,000
When the costume is more complicated and clever, the simulation will take longer.

71
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:22,000
If you want to stop the simulation, please press the control button again or click the simulation button.

72
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:32,000
Please save your project file, and we will continue to use it after the next tutorial.

